Translation patch: `FromRow::from_row` (default method)

Change: `panic!("Couldn't convert {:?} to type {}. (see FromRow documentation)", row, type_name::<Self>())` becomes `panic!("Couldn't convert the row to the requested type. (see FromRow documentation)")`, and the `type_name` import is dropped.
Why: Formatting the row uses `Debug for Row` / `Debug for Value` (`str::pattern`, which Aeneas cannot translate), and `type_name` is an intrinsic Aeneas does not model; formatting is out of scope (as in patch 47).
Behaviour: Identical except for the text of the panic message: it panics in exactly the same cases (`from_row_opt` returns `Err`). (As in patch 47's note, upstream formatting can itself overflow in `Debug for Value::Time`; the patched copy panics normally there.)

diff --git a/src/row/convert/mod.rs b/src/row/convert/mod.rs
index 6f544cf..0428efd 100644
--- a/src/row/convert/mod.rs
+++ b/src/row/convert/mod.rs
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ use crate::{
     },
 };
 
-use std::{any::type_name, error::Error, fmt};
+use std::{error::Error, fmt};
 
 pub mod frunk;
 
@@ -81,11 +81,9 @@ pub trait FromRow {
     {
         match Self::from_row_opt(row) {
             Ok(x) => x,
-            Err(FromRowError(row)) => panic!(
-                "Couldn't convert {:?} to type {}. (see FromRow documentation)",
